Two roads (a, b) and (c, d) will intersect inside the ring if the intervals [min(a,b), max(a,b)] and [min(c,d), max(c,d)] are interleaved (i.e., one endpoint of one interval is between the endpoints of the other interval). Similarly, they will intersect outside the ring if they "cross" when drawn outside.

